# systemd refuses nothing for a CRLF unit file -- it just carries the \r INTO
# the value, so Environment="PATH=/usr/bin\r" silently breaks every lookup.
# The repo has core.autocrlf=true on the Windows box these were written on, so
# say it explicitly rather than rely on the default.
*.service text eol=lf
*.timer   text eol=lf
*.conf    text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf
*.py     text eol=lf
# zalo-health.ps1 carries Vietnamese and emoji in its alert text, and Windows
# PowerShell 5.1 decides a script's encoding by BOM alone: with no BOM it reads
# the file as the system ANSI codepage (Windows-1252 on the deploy box), which
# turns "🔴 Zalo bot DOWN —" into "ðŸ”´ Zalo bot DOWN â€”" in the delivered
# alert. The BOM is therefore load-bearing content -- git leaves it alone, but
# any redeploy that rewrites this file must keep it (Set-Content -Encoding utf8
# in PS 5.1 writes one; PS 7+ needs utf8BOM).
*.ps1    text eol=crlf
